; Chase camera, FACING FORWARD.
;
; The original basis had the camera looking down world -Z while the cart runs
; toward +Z. A headless probe of the real scene measured dot(forward, direction
; to the next obstacle) = -0.86: the entire track ahead, and the cart itself,
; were BEHIND the camera. The player was watching the tunnel they had already
; passed, which is why the cart was never in frame and why hazards were
; impossible to read - they arrived from off-screen behind.
;
; Basis below: forward (0,-0.407,0.914) = down +Z pitched 24 degrees down,
; right (-1,0,0), up (0,0.914,0.407). Position is 7.5 behind and 3.2 above the
; cart, so the cart sits in the lower third of frame as in every reference.
[node name="Camera3D" type="Camera3D" parent="Cart"]
transform = Transform3D(-1, 0, 0, 0, 0.914, 0.407, 0, 0.407, -0.914, 0, 3.2, -7.5)

; Graybox lighting. Without a light and an environment a 3D scene renders unlit/black in the web export.
[node name="WorldEnvironment" type="WorldEnvironment" parent="."]
environment = SubResource("Environment_runner")

[node name="Sun" type="DirectionalLight3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 0.6, 0.8, 0, -0.8, 0.6, 0, 12, -4)
light_energy = 0.75
shadow_enabled = true
